{%- comment -%}
  AJ About — the origin story, on a CRT.

  EVERY WORD IS A SETTING, NOT MARKUP. This is the page most likely to be
  reworded on a whim, and copy baked into a section means a git push and a
  theme deploy to change a comma. The defaults below are Alex's text, verbatim.

  THE PIXEL FACE DOES NOT SET THE STORY, and that is the whole design.
  aj-brand.css is explicit: "Ohpixel is a pixel grid that turns to mush in
  lowercase or in sentences", and every existing use uppercases it "because
  Ohpixel is drawn for capitals and loses its grid in mixed case". Five hundred
  words of origin story in it would be unreadable at any screen size.

  So the faces split by JOB, the way the brand file already splits them:

      Ohpixel   the terminal chrome — the h1, boot lines, pull quote, tagline.
                Short, uppercase, structural. Exactly its shape.
      Flashy    the optional display heading, which is copy we wrote. Blank by
                default since 4 Aug: it competed with the monitor for the top
                of the page, and the monitor is the reason anyone scrolls.
      Archivo   the story. Ninety percent of the words, as everywhere else.

  That is what makes the monitor work: it LOOKS like a terminal because the
  chrome is pixels and phosphor, while the part you actually read is set in the
  face built for reading.

  THE SCREEN HAS NO FIXED ASPECT RATIO. A monitor drawn as a fixed shape is
  exactly what breaks on a phone — the text either shrinks to nothing or
  overflows the bezel. Here the "monitor" is a treatment (padding, border,
  glow, scanlines) on a panel that grows with its content, so it is correct at
  every width by construction rather than by breakpoint.

  SCANLINES ARE A BACKGROUND, NEVER AN OVERLAY. Striping a translucent layer
  OVER the text is the obvious implementation and it drags contrast down on
  every other row. They are painted on the screen's own background instead, so
  the copy sits cleanly above them at full strength.

  MOTION IS THE BOOT SEQUENCE AND NOTHING ELSE. The lines print one at a time,
  once, and then the page is static — re-reading should never mean re-watching.
  The cursor blinks only while the boot is running and goes solid after. All of
  it is skipped under prefers-reduced-motion, and because the lines are in the
  DOM already, a browser with JS off shows the whole thing immediately rather
  than an empty screen.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign fallback = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0731/4512/2918/files/retro_pc.H01.png?v=1785860292'
-%}

<div
  class="aj-about color-{{ s.color_scheme }}"
  style="padding-block-start: {{ s.padding-block-start }}px; padding-block-end: {{ s.padding-block-end }}px;"
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div class="aj-about__inner">
    {%- comment -%}
      The eyebrow carries the <h1>, not the display heading below it.

      With the big heading removed the page would otherwise have no h1 at all —
      bad for search and worse for anyone navigating by headings. "About us" is
      a perfectly good page heading; it just does not need to be 56px to do the
      job. The optional heading is an h2 so adding one back later cannot
      produce two h1s.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
      <h1 class="aj-about__eyebrow">{{ s.eyebrow | escape }}</h1>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="aj-about__heading">{{ s.heading | escape }}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The phosphor colour is set INLINE rather than in the stylesheet block
      below, because Shopify does not run Liquid inside {% stylesheet %} — a
      `{{ }}` in there ships to the browser as literal text. Same reason the
      padding is on the wrapper.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      THE MACHINE IS NOW THE SAME PHOTOGRAPH THE HOMEPAGE USES, and the story
      sits BELOW it rather than inside it.

      That split is the whole trick. A screen that is a fixed region of a
      raster cannot grow, so five hundred words inside the glass would either
      shrink to nothing or overflow the bezel — the exact failure that made the
      drawn monitor necessary in the first place. Putting three short lines on
      the real screen and the story on a panel underneath gets the look of the
      homepage teaser with none of that: the image carries the atmosphere, the
      panel carries the words, and both are the same glass.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="aj-about__machine" style="--aj-crt-phosphor: {{ s.phosphor }};">
      {%- if s.image != blank -%}
        {{
          s.image
          | image_url: width: 1400
          | image_tag:
            widths: '400, 600, 800, 1100, 1400',
            sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 34rem, 88vw',
            alt: s.image_alt,
            class: 'aj-about__img',
            loading: 'eager'
        }}
      {%- else -%}
        <img
          class="aj-about__img"
          src="{{ fallback }}&width=1400"
          srcset="{{ fallback }}&width=600 600w, {{ fallback }}&width=900 900w, {{ fallback }}&width=1400 1400w"
          sizes="(min-width: 750px) 34rem, 88vw"
          alt="{{ s.image_alt | escape }}"
          width="2048"
          height="2048"
        >
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if s.screen_lines != blank -%}
        <div class="aj-about__glass" aria-hidden="true">
          {%- assign mlines = s.screen_lines | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
          {%- for line in mlines -%}
            {%- assign mtrim = line | strip -%}
            {%- if mtrim != blank -%}
              <p class="aj-about__gline">{{ mtrim | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          <p class="aj-about__gline"><span class="aj-about__gcursor"></span></p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="aj-crt" style="--aj-crt-phosphor: {{ s.phosphor }}; --aj-crt-screen: {{ s.screen_color }};">
      <div class="aj-crt__screen">
        {%- if s.boot_lines != blank -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            aria-hidden: this is decorative chrome, and a screen reader
            announcing "greater-than LOADING ORIGIN dot TXT" before the story
            is noise rather than atmosphere.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="aj-crt__boot" data-aj-boot aria-hidden="true">
            {%- assign lines = s.boot_lines | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
            {%- for line in lines -%}
              {%- assign trimmed = line | strip -%}
              {%- if trimmed != blank -%}
                <p class="aj-crt__bootline">{{ trimmed | escape }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.lead != blank -%}
          <div class="aj-crt__lead rte">{{ s.lead }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.body_1 != blank -%}
          <div class="aj-crt__body rte">{{ s.body_1 }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.pull_quote != blank -%}
          <p class="aj-crt__pull">{{ s.pull_quote | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.body_2 != blank -%}
          <div class="aj-crt__body rte">{{ s.body_2 }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.signoff != blank -%}
          <p class="aj-crt__signoff">
            {{- s.signoff | escape -}}
            <span class="aj-crt__cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

    </div>

    {%- if s.tagline != blank -%}
      <p class="aj-about__tagline">{{ s.tagline | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.primary_text != blank or s.secondary_text != blank -%}
      <div class="aj-about__actions">
        {%- if s.primary_text != blank -%}
          <a class="aj-about__btn aj-about__btn--primary" href="{{ s.primary_link | default: '/' }}">
            {{- s.primary_text | escape -}}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.secondary_text != blank -%}
          <a class="aj-about__btn aj-about__btn--ghost" href="{{ s.secondary_link | default: '/' }}">
            {{- s.secondary_text | escape -}}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  (function () {
    var script = document.currentScript;
    if (!script) return;
    var root = script.parentElement;
    var boot = root && root.querySelector('[data-aj-boot]');
    if (!boot) return;

    /* Reduced motion gets the finished state, not a slower animation. The
       lines are already in the DOM and already visible; this only opts IN to
       the sequence, so doing nothing here is the correct fallback for
       reduced-motion AND for JS being unavailable. */
    var reduce = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
    if (reduce && reduce.matches) return;

    var lines = boot.querySelectorAll('.aj-crt__bootline');
    for (var i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {
      lines[i].style.animationDelay = i * 0.42 + 's';
    }
    boot.setAttribute('data-aj-boot', 'running');

    /* The cursor stops blinking once the log has finished printing. Idle
       motion that never resolves is the thing people ask you to turn off. */
    var done = lines.length * 0.42 + 0.6;
    var cursor = root.querySelector('.aj-crt__cursor');
    if (cursor) {
      cursor.classList.add('is-blinking');
      window.setTimeout(function () {
        cursor.classList.remove('is-blinking');
      }, done * 1000);
    }
  })();
</script>

{% stylesheet %}
  .aj-about {
    padding-inline: 1.25rem;
  }

  /* WIDE ENOUGH TO READ AS A MONITOR, which is a different constraint from
     the one this started with. At 62ch the shell was a tall narrow column —
     correct for prose, but nothing shaped like that has ever been a CRT, and
     it never fit on a screen. 48rem is roughly 1.5x wider, which also cuts the
     shell's HEIGHT by about a third for the same words, so far more of the
     machine is visible at once.

     The reading measure moves INSIDE the screen instead (see __lead/__body
     below). Widening the box and letting the text follow it to 85 characters
     would have traded one problem for a worse one. */
  .aj-about__inner {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .aj-about__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--aj-price-act, #7a3fa0);
  }

  /* Flashy, because this is a heading we wrote — the same rule aj-brand.css
     applies to every other heading of ours. Weight 400: Flashy has one weight
     and the theme's 700 renders it synthetically emboldened. */
  .aj-about__heading {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* ---- the monitor ------------------------------------------------------ */

  /*
    THE CASE IS GONE — it is a photograph now, above this panel. What remains
    is the glass: the story sits on a screen that matches the one in the image,
    so the page reads as the same machine continued rather than as two designs.
  */
  .aj-crt {
    --aj-crt-screen: #0b100c;
    --aj-crt-phosphor: #5cf08a;
    --aj-crt-text: #d6f5e0;
    --aj-crt-dim: rgb(214 245 224 / 0.62);

    position: relative;
    margin-block-start: 1.5rem;
  }

  /*
    THE HALO A TUBE THROWS ON THE WALL BEHIND IT.

    A CRT is a light source, and the one thing a flat drawing of one never gets
    is that it spills. This is that spill: a soft ellipse of the phosphor
    colour, blurred wide, breathing slowly.

    SUBTLETY IS THE ENTIRE SPEC. It moves between 0.30 and 0.52 opacity over
    six seconds — wide enough to notice if you look at it, narrow enough that
    nothing on the page appears to move. A pulse you can consciously watch is
    a distraction sitting next to five hundred words somebody is trying to
    read; the effect wanted here is "this thing is on", not "this thing is
    animating".

    z-index: -1 puts it behind the beige without hiding it behind the PAGE,
    because .aj-crt is positioned but sets no z-index of its own.

    Derived from --aj-crt-phosphor, so changing the screen colour changes the
    colour of the light it throws. Green screen, green wall.
  */
  .aj-crt::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    z-index: -1;
    inset: -6% -8%;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(
      ellipse at center,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--aj-crt-phosphor) 34%, transparent) 0%,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--aj-crt-phosphor) 10%, transparent) 45%,
      transparent 72%
    );
    filter: blur(38px);
    opacity: 0.3;
    pointer-events: none;
    animation: aj-crt-breathe 6s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  @keyframes aj-crt-breathe {
    0%,
    100% {
      opacity: 0.3;
      transform: scale(1);
    }

    50% {
      opacity: 0.52;
      transform: scale(1.035);
    }
  }

  .aj-crt__screen {
    /* NO aspect-ratio. The panel grows with its content, which is what makes
       this survive a phone without a single breakpoint. */
    padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem 2rem;

    border-radius: 14px;
    color: var(--aj-crt-text);

    /* Scanlines live in the BACKGROUND, behind the copy — see the note at the
       top of this file. */
    background-color: var(--aj-crt-screen);
    background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0.035) 0 1px,
      transparent 1px 3px
    );

    /* Two shadows doing different jobs. The inset vignette is what sells the
       glass — darkening toward the corners is how a real tube falls off. The
       outer one is the bloom the phosphor throws onto the bezel around it,
       which is the thing that actually reads as "glowing" rather than "dark
       rectangle". Both are shadows, so neither distorts the text. */
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 80px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.62),
      inset 0 0 26px color-mix(in srgb, var(--aj-crt-phosphor) 12%, transparent),
      0 0 34px color-mix(in srgb, var(--aj-crt-phosphor) 22%, transparent);
  }

  /* ---- boot sequence ----------------------------------------------------- */

  .aj-crt__boot {
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
    padding-block-end: 1.25rem;
    border-block-end: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.12);
  }

  .aj-crt__bootline {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--aj-crt-phosphor);
    text-shadow: 0 0 14px color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 45%, transparent);
  }

  /* Default state is VISIBLE. The animation is opted into by script, so no-JS
     and reduced-motion both land on the finished screen rather than a blank
     one. */
  [data-aj-boot='running'] .aj-crt__bootline {
    opacity: 0;
    animation: aj-crt-print 0.01s linear forwards;
  }

  @keyframes aj-crt-print {
    to {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }

  /* ---- the story --------------------------------------------------------- */

  /* Archivo, deliberately. The opening paragraph is set larger than the body
     and lighter than the heading — a bridge between the two rather than a
     third competing size. */
  /* The measure lives here now, not on the shell. Left-aligned rather than
     centred: a terminal starts its text at the left margin and lets the rest
     of the line go dark, and the pull quote's rule below only makes sense
     against a left edge. */
  .aj-crt__lead,
  .aj-crt__body,
  .aj-crt__pull,
  .aj-crt__boot {
    max-width: 64ch;
  }

  .aj-crt__lead p {
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .aj-crt__body p {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--aj-crt-dim);
  }

  .aj-crt__body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* The pull quote is the one place a long-ish line goes into the pixel face,
     and it is uppercase and short enough to hold its grid. Left-aligned with a
     rule rather than centred: centring would break the reading column the rest
     of the screen depends on. */
  .aj-crt__pull {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 0.9rem 0 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--aj-crt-phosphor);
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--aj-crt-phosphor);
    text-shadow: 0 0 18px color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 40%, transparent);
  }

  .aj-crt__signoff {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--aj-crt-phosphor);
    text-shadow: 0 0 14px color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 45%, transparent);
  }

  .aj-crt__cursor {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.6em;
    height: 1em;
    margin-inline-start: 0.35em;
    background: var(--aj-crt-phosphor);
    vertical-align: -0.12em;
  }

  .aj-crt__cursor.is-blinking {
    animation: aj-crt-blink 1s steps(1, end) infinite;
  }

  @keyframes aj-crt-blink {
    50% {
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }

  /* ---- the machine, same photograph as the homepage --------------------- */

  .aj-about__machine {
    container-type: inline-size;
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .aj-about__img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* Measured off the PNG: x 311-1069, y 604-1180 of 2048, aspect 1.32. */
  .aj-about__glass {
    position: absolute;
    left: 15.19%;
    top: 29.49%;
    width: 37.01%;
    height: 28.12%;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.4cqi;
    padding: 0 2cqi;
    overflow: hidden;
    background:
      radial-gradient(
        ellipse at 50% 55%,
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--aj-crt-phosphor) 12%, transparent) 0%,
        transparent 70%
      ),
      repeating-linear-gradient(
        to bottom,
        rgb(255 255 255 / 0.045) 0 1px,
        transparent 1px 3px
      );
  }

  /* cqi so the type tracks the image's width — a px size would spill out of
     the glass the moment the image narrowed. */
  .aj-about__gline {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 2.15cqi;
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--aj-crt-phosphor);
    text-shadow: 0 0 1.4cqi color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 55%, transparent);
  }

  .aj-about__gcursor {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 1.4cqi;
    height: 2.2cqi;
    background: var(--aj-crt-phosphor);
    box-shadow: 0 0 1.4cqi color-mix(in srgb, var(--aj-crt-phosphor) 55%, transparent);
    animation: aj-about-blink 1.1s steps(1, end) infinite;
  }

  @keyframes aj-about-blink {
    50% {
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }

  /* ---- below the monitor -------------------------------------------------- */

  /* Ink on yellow, never yellow type. aj-brand.css measured it: yellow on
     white is 1.32:1 and fails WCAG 1.4.3 at any size; ink on that yellow is
     11.17:1. The accent is a background here or it is not used. */
  .aj-about__tagline {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    border-radius: var(--aj-tile-radius, 8px);
    background: var(--aj-price-grab, #ffe000);
    color: var(--aj-price-read, #282828);
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .aj-about__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-block-start: 1.5rem;
  }

  .aj-about__btn {
    flex: 1 1 12rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--aj-tile-radius, 8px);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: center;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
  }

  .aj-about__btn--primary {
    background: var(--aj-price-act, #7a3fa0);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .aj-about__btn--ghost {
    border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.25);
    color: inherit;
  }

  @media (hover: hover) {
    .aj-about__btn:hover {
      opacity: 0.88;
    }
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    /* The bezel thins rather than the screen shrinking — chrome is what gives
       way on a small screen, never the reading area. */
    .aj-crt__screen {
      padding: 1.35rem 1.1rem 1.6rem;
    }

    .aj-crt__lead p {
      font-size: 1.0625rem;
    }

    /* Ohpixel needs to come down harder than the body face does: a pixel grid
       that lands between whole pixels is where it starts to look broken. */
    .aj-crt__pull {
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    }

    .aj-crt__bootline {
      font-size: 0.6875rem;
    }

    .aj-about__gline {
      font-size: 2.6cqi;
    }

    .aj-about__tagline {
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
    }

    .aj-about__btn {
      flex-basis: 100%;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .aj-crt__bootline,
    .aj-about__gcursor,
    .aj-crt__cursor.is-blinking {
      animation: none !important;
      opacity: 1 !important;
    }

    /* The glow STAYS, it just stops breathing. Reduced motion is a request to
       remove movement, not to remove the design — deleting the halo would
       serve a different page to the people who asked for fewer animations. */
    .aj-crt::after {
      animation: none;
      opacity: 0.4;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AJ About",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The origin story, framed as a CRT terminal. Founders stay anonymous — 'two coworkers', no names, no photos."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "About us" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Optional. Left blank the page leads straight into the monitor, which is how it is set now."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "The machine" },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Computer image",
      "info": "Must be face-on with the screen square to camera. Falls back to the uploaded retro PC if empty."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "image_alt", "label": "Image alt text", "default": "A beige 1990s desktop computer" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "screen_lines",
      "label": "Text on the screen",
      "info": "One line each, uppercased automatically. Three lines maximum — the glass is small and a cursor is added after them.",
      "default": "C:\\> ORIGIN.TXT\nTwo guys.\nOne deal a day."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Story panel" },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "phosphor",
      "label": "Phosphor",
      "info": "The glow colour. Every shadow on the screen derives from this, so changing it recolours the whole monitor.",
      "default": "#5cf08a"
    },
    { "type": "color", "id": "screen_color", "label": "Screen", "default": "#0b100c" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "boot_lines",
      "label": "Boot sequence",
      "info": "One line each. Prints line by line on load. Uppercased automatically — keep them short.",
      "default": "The Yoink Co. Terminal v1.0\n> Loading origin.txt ...\n> OK"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "lead",
      "label": "Opening paragraph",
      "default": "<p>We're a couple of '90s kids. We missed the dot-com boom by about a decade, came of age dodging recessions and pandemics, and have basically spent our whole adult lives being told the timing's bad. So instead of waiting around for a better hand, we decided to have some fun with the one we've got.</p>"
